' ── DECIDED 2026-11-14: CONTINUITY FOLLOWS SBX; THE STOPGAP ENDS THE LEAK ─
' The owner's three decisions, taken after the stopgap below was built:
'   1. DIRECTION (DECIDED): sbx's model. One named sandbox per (harness,
'      workspace), kept and re-attached; history on a live host directory
'      per (harness, workspace). The per-file state sync, volume@1 and the
'      retained-engine special case go: hermes's live bind and OpenCode's
'      retained engine become the rule. The owner: "Note the hermes and
'      opencode exceptions in _plans/ to look for standardization". That
'      plan is _spec/_plans/session-continuity.puml; nothing here builds it.
'   2. VM-LOCAL (DECIDED): claude's sessions/ is VM-local, never carried
'      between VMs; daemon.lock, daemon/ and jobs/ likewise. statsig/ and
'      shell-snapshots/ stay VM-local, as the volume-era skip had them.
'   3. THE LEAK (DECIDED): the stopgap drops the five volume@1 from the
'      vendored claude kit (upstream sbx/claude dropped them in 2.1.317) and
'      carries projects/<workspace keys> and todos/ through its scoped
'      newer-wins copy. The stranded volumes and the host's
'      ~/.proveo/.claude/sessions stay untouched for the owner.
' NOW, on the claudecode manifest's .claude mount (harness-manifest-schema):
'   state:     [projects, todos]
'              → PROVEO_STATE_DIRS=".claude/projects|.claude/projects;
'                .claude/todos|.claude/todos" (proveohome.StateSet)
'   transient: [sessions, statsig, shell-snapshots, daemon.lock,
'              daemon.status.json, daemon.log, daemon, jobs]
'              → the skip field of PROVEO_CONFIG_DIRS; jobs replaces jobs/*/tmp
' proveo_sync_state acts on PROVEO_STATE_DIRS, and _proveo_config_skips
' prunes each of its entries under the synced root, then the deny and
' transient names. Pass 1's rules are unchanged: newer wins by direction,
' staging + rename, the restore marker, the save refusal, the projects/ keys.
' An env with no PROVEO_STATE_DIRS falls back to pass 1's discovery (row C
' below: a sandbox an older CLI created on this image, its kit still
' mounting the five volumes). _proveo_volume_dirs lists the /dev/* mounts
' under $HOME from /proc/mounts; the state sync takes them minus sessions,
' statsig and shell-snapshots, and _proveo_config_skips prunes every one.
' _proveo_volume_state_dirs is deleted. A sandbox this CLI creates mounts no
' volume, so the fallback finds nothing in it.
' The state dirs travel in their own variable, not in the shared skip field,
' so a lib that predates PROVEO_STATE_DIRS still carries projects/ and todos/
' through its config sync (row B below) rather than through neither sync.
' daemon.status.json (supervisorPid, supervisorProcStart) and daemon.log
' joined the VM-local set after a check of pass 2 measured both crossing;
' they are the daemon's per-VM files beside daemon.lock. [Inference] The
' crossing cost little, since Claude Code 2.1.323 checks that pid with
' kill(pid,0) and its start time.
' Pinned: TestProjectsAndTodosRoundTripOnPlainDirectories,
' TestVMLocalPathsNeverCrossEitherSync, TestAConfigSaveNoLongerCarriesProjects,
' TestConfigSyncLeavesTheStateDirsToTheStateSync,
' TestWithoutStateDirsTheKitVolumesTravelAsState (row C),
' TestClaudeCodeDeclaresItsStateDirsAndItsVMLocalPaths,
' TestStateSetEncodesEachSyncedMountsStateDirs,
' TestStatePathsAreLiteralDirsInsideASyncedMount. MEASURED in golang:1.26.7
' against origin/main's lib: the round-trip, config-save and config-skip
' tests fail. The VM-local test passes on any lib once the manifest lists
' the paths, and fails on every assertion with the old [jobs/*/tmp] list;
' with pass 2's list it fails on daemon.status.json and daemon.log alone.
' The row C test fails on pass 2's lib, which read no /proc/mounts: the cut
' copy took its name, the save cut the host from 376000 to 4096 bytes with
' rc 0, and sessions/ crossed both ways.
'
' ── WHY sessions/ IS VM-LOCAL (decision 2's evidence) ─────────────────────
' MEASURED 2026-11-14 in the Claude Code 2.1.323 bundle and the host store:
' sessions/ holds one <pid>.json per RUNNING session plus a <pid>.<hash>.key
' peer token; --resume and `claude -c` list projects/, not sessions/. In a
' VM no record is pruned (IS_SANDBOX=1 declines the registry sweep), and the
' record's pidDomain, linux::pid:[<ns inode>] with an empty machine-id, is
' the same in every proveo VM (one value covered 21 records over 9 days). A
' shared store therefore fills every VM with dead records, and a record from
' an older image's domain counts as held elsewhere: `claude -c` skips or
' refuses that transcript ("registered from another machine or container").
' The host store held 78 records, one cut mid-write, and 81 keys.
' daemon.lock carries a pid with no pidDomain; daemon.status.json,
' daemon.log, daemon/ (roster, control key) and jobs/ (14 entries) are the
' same daemon's per-VM state.
'
' ── THE VOLUME LEAK: CAUSE AND EVIDENCE (decision 3) ──────────────────────
' MEASURED 2026-11-14 on the owner's host, read-only: the sbx datastore held
' 1,710 records labelled com.docker.sandbox.persistent-volume=true. 1,360
' name a kit identity under ~/.local/state/proveo/runs/<sid>/sbx/kit/, and
' 350 come from test temp dirs. They span 275 sandbox names; one stable name
' held 75 volumes over 15 kit identities (5 x 15). [Inference] About 91 GiB:
' du counted 95,245,344 KB of sandbox-volume-<id>.img; not re-measured here.
' Cause: the vendored claude kit declared five volume@1, and sandbox.go
' builds KitDir under each run's RunDir, so every run is a new kit identity.
' sbx v0.50 keeps volumes on rm and reattaches one only when the sandbox
' name AND the kit source match, and no local command removes them
' (docker/sbx-releases#842). Each claudecode create stranded five more.
' Upstream: sbx/claude:2.1.267 declared the five; 2.1.317 (2026-11-04) and
' :latest declare none, and dropped the startup chown that re-owned them.
' NOW: the vendored kit declares no volume@1 and no re-own hook (DELTA 3),
' so a run strands nothing. Pinned: TestNoVendoredKitDeclaresAVolume.
'
' ── WHAT STAYS ON THE HOST, UNTOUCHED, FOR THE OWNER ──────────────────────
' Nothing in this change deletes or rewrites:
'   the 1,710 stranded volume records and their images in sbx's datastore;
'   ~/.proveo/.claude/sessions, daemon.lock, daemon/ and jobs/: transient,
'     unlike deny, never scrubs the host's copy;
'   ~/.proveo/.claude/statsig and shell-snapshots, where a past copy left them.
' A sandbox an older image runs still writes its sessions/ there (row A).
'
' ── OLD SANDBOXES UNDER THIS CLI (MEASURED, compat.sh in debian:13-slim) ──
' A sandbox keeps the image, kit and create-time env it was made with; this
' CLI picks only the argv. The lib that saves is the sandbox's own.
'   row  lib          kit, env             argv                  host gets, rc
'   A    origin/main  volumes, old env     SaveStateArgs         projects todos sessions, 0
'   A'   origin/main  volumes, old env     GuardedSaveStateArgs  nothing, 3
'   B    origin/main  no volume, new env   SaveStateArgs         projects todos (config), 0
'   C    this lib     volumes, old env     SaveStateArgs         projects todos, 0
'   D    this lib     no volume, new env   SaveStateArgs         projects todos, 0
' A is a kept sandbox an older CLI made. Its kit and env differ from this
' CLI's. A non-interactive run retires a stopped one (the retire saves
' first, and F2 keeps it on a failed save) and lets a live one run on
' unchanged, whose teardown then saves with its own lib, sessions/ included,
' as that image always did. A headed run asks about both, Keep first: Keep
' on a live one runs on as above, Keep on a stopped one ends the run with
' nothing saved, and Replace retires it. A retire's `sbx exec` boots a
' stopped sandbox, and that image's seed restore runs beside the save under
' the shared lock; when the restore goes first it reverts guest files newer
' than the host's (F4, which xws.sh measured on that lib). compat.sh did not
' model that boot. [Inference] Only turns written after the sandbox's last
' teardown save are at risk. A' is `proveo rm` on
' the same sandbox: D6 skips an image that predates the restore wait, says
' so, and removes. [Inference] A pass-1 image passes the guard and saves
' through its volume discovery. B is a stale local image under this CLI:
' its state sync finds no block device, and its config sync, which ignores
' PROVEO_STATE_DIRS, carries projects/ and todos/ whole-store while still
' skipping the transient names. C is an older CLI with this image: no
' PROVEO_STATE_DIRS, so the lib falls back to the volume dirs (NOW above).
' The state sync carries projects/ (scoped) and todos/, and the config sync
' prunes all five volumes, so sessions/, statsig/ and shell-snapshots/ stay
' in the VM. C's old env marks only jobs/*/tmp transient, so daemon.lock,
' daemon.status.json, daemon.log, daemon/ and jobs/ still cross by config
' sync, as on origin/main. MEASURED (rowc-mounts.sh, docker volumes at the
' five paths in debian:13-slim): the restore brought this workspace's key,
' todos/ and settings.json and no sessions/; the save carried the turn and
' no sessions/ or statsig/. Before the fallback, MEASURED by the check's
' rowc.sh on a 2 MiB volume: the config restore stopped at 2,093,056 bytes,
' the save cut the host file from 4,000,001 to 2,093,056 bytes with rc 0,
' and the host's sessions/1200.json entered the VM. [Inference] B's
' whole-store config restore can outrun the agent's 30s gate on a large
' store. Both rows end once CLI and image carry this change.
