'       D3: A RESTORE THAT FAILS FOR A LASTING REASON REFUSES EVERY LATER
'       SAVE. MEASURED (rc 1, no marker, every later save refused): a host
'       directory where the guest holds a file, a host file with mode 0000,
'       a newline in a file name (the plan is line-based), and 40,000 files
'       in one directory. A kept sandbox that stays running never re-runs
'       its seed, and a stopped one fails the same restore on each boot, so
'       "the next run saves it again" and "`proveo rm` tries again" never
'       succeed. Every such fix line now also names `sbx rm --force <name>`,
'       which deletes it with the state only in it. The 40,000-file case is
'       fixed: one mv got every name of a directory and exceeded the exec
'       argument limit (0 of 40,000 landed); the names now go through
'       `xargs -0`. The other three stay lasting failures, and the save's
'       refusal keeps the host copy whole. Pinned:
'       TestARestorePastTheArgumentLimitPlacesEveryFile (4,000 names under
'       a 512 KiB stack, whose argument limit is the 128 KiB floor;
'       MEASURED before the fix: 0 of 4,000 placed).
'   F4  RESTORE OVERWROTE NEWER GUEST DATA. _proveo_changed_files copied on
'       any size or mtime difference and never asked which side is newer.
'       MEASURED (xws.sh): a kept volume went from a0|a2-unsaved to a0 on a
'       boot restore. Every boot of a kept sandbox restores, and a teardown,
'       retire or rm exec on a stopped sandbox is such a boot.
'       NOW: _proveo_state_plan decides by direction. A restore replaces a
'       file only when the host's mtime is strictly newer; a save replaces
'       one when the guest's is newer, or when the guest wrote it in the last
'       5s and the host's is not newer (the same-tick section below).
'       Pinned: TestStateRestoreNeverRevertsANewerGuestTurn.
'   F5  TWO SANDBOXES IN DIFFERENT WORKSPACES REVERTED EACH OTHER. Restore
'       copied the whole store, and save copied any file that differed.
'       MEASURED (xws.sh): wsA=a0|a1-turn-by-A became wsA=a0 after B's save.
'       NOW: restore of .claude/projects copies only this run's entries (the
'       key section below), and save is newer-wins, so a stale copy a volume
